WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.214
Lab 2 runs the inventory against your own
test tenant, in the worldwide or G C C

2
00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:10.788
cloud, with a test Azure subscription,
never production, and with fictional people.

3
00:00:10.788 --> 00:00:12.525
The run only reads.

4
00:00:12.525 --> 00:00:15.092
You register a reader
app with a certificate,

5
00:00:15.092 --> 00:00:18.908
and grant it the five Graph
application permissions from step two,

6
00:00:18.908 --> 00:00:22.100
with admin consent, and Reader
on the test subscription.

7
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.456
Then you run the inventory, cross-check
it against the admin center's download,

8
00:00:26.456 --> 00:00:28.975
and check the two things
the fixture assumed.

9
00:00:28.975 --> 00:00:32.788
To back it out, remove the Reader
assignment, the five permissions,

10
00:00:32.788 --> 00:00:37.237
the app registration and its certificate,
and delete the test output folder,

11
00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.850
which names the tenant's
privileged holders.

12
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:45.500
The path's authors haven't run Lab 2;
the workbook's Lab 2 gives every step.
